        "original_id": "545655db-87fd-5115-a4fe-c81ab59e0579",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Cases: Glassroth v. Moore; Maddox and Howard v. Moore\n- People: Roy S. Moore\n- Organizations: Alabama Supreme Court; Foundation for Moral Law\n- Places: Alabama Judicial Building; Montgomery, Alabama\n- Topics: Ten Commandments monument\n\nFacts:\n- In 2002, Glassroth v. Moore, CV-01-T-1268-N, was reported at 229 F. Supp. 2d 1290 in the Middle District of Alabama.\n- In 2002, Maddox and Howard v. Moore, CV-01-T-1269-N, was identified as a companion case to Glassroth v. Moore.\n- Glassroth v. Moore and Maddox and Howard v. Moore concerned then-Alabama Supreme Court Chief Justice Roy S. Moore.\n- Glassroth v. Moore and Maddox and Howard v. Moore concerned a stone monument of the Ten Commandments in the rotunda of the Alabama Judicial Building in Montgomery, Alabama.\n- Roy S. Moore is the founder and president of the Foundation for Moral Law.",
